-- A link with arguments ends a method chain, so `.collect` here attaches to
-- the closure argument. That used to transpile to
-- `xs.into_iter().map((|x| x * 2).collect, ())`, which only rustc refused.
-- A closure has no fields, so the reading can never be meant: the parser
-- refuses it and names the bracketing that continues the chain instead.
doubled : Vec<u32> -> Vec<u32>
doubled xs = xs.into_iter ().map (\x -> x * 2).collect ()
